(a) Food. Have at least fifty (50) percent of its total annual gross sales be the sale of prepared meals or food, if it permits Sunday alcohol sales; if it does not permit Sunday alcohol sales, a beer garden is required to meet the thirty (30) percent food requirement as required in section 3-126. A beer garden can have an on-site kitchen or can use the provisions of section 3-80 to satisfy this requirement;
(b) Have an open-air area (roofed or unroofed) to provide alcohol service and (if desired) food service. The beer garden may also have an indoor service area (if desired, no smaller than five hundred (500) square feet). A beer garden shall have an associated permanent structure on-site to provide restrooms, secure storage of alcohol, refrigeration and waste-disposal facilities, the total area for all facilities and open space shall not exceed two thousand (2,000) sf;
(c) The open-air area must be separated from non-licensed property and public rights-of-way by a fence, barrier, vegetation or similar demarcation. The applicant will be required to demonstrate how the open-air area is to be separated from the adjacent areas, how any nuisance towards adjacent properties will be mitigated, and how patrons will be prevented from leaving the permitted area with an alcoholic beverage. Sales through drive-thru windows or other windows or doors to the street, sidewalk or vehicles are prohibited.
(d) Location restrictions. The property must be located in a commercially zoned district as indicated in the Unified Development Code. The alcohol service area of any beer garden must be located one hundred (100) feet or more from residentially zoned and used parcels (under the City of Powder Springs Unified Development Code). If entertainment in the form of music, bands, groups, amplification systems or loud noise of any kind is offered in a beer garden, the alcohol service area shall be located two hundred and fifty (250) feet or more from a residential zoned and used property. Distances shall be measured from the point of the beer garden area closest to a residential zone to the closest property line of that property with a residential use. Amplified sound or alcohol sales shall not be permitted during the hours of operation of day cares or schools within five hundred (500) feet of the beer garden.
(e) Roofing or enclosing the open-air area with a tent may require inspection and approval from the state or local fire marshal. Applicants are advised to consult with the appropriate official.
(Ord. No. 2023-009, § 1 (Exh. A), 10-16-23)

