The building official shall hold the following certifications:
(1) If inspecting for compliance with the International Building Code or the portion of the International Residential Code for One- and Two-Family Dwellings, the inspector shall be certified from the International Code Council (ICC) as a building inspector;
(2) If inspecting for compliance with the National Electrical Code or the electrical portion of the International Residential Code for One- and Two-Family Dwellings, the inspector shall be certified from the International Code Council (ICC) as a residential electrical inspector or an electrical contractor license from the state construction industry licensing board;
(3) If inspecting for compliance with the National Electrical Code of nonresidential buildings, the inspector shall be certified from the International Code Council (ICC) as a commercial electrical inspector or an electrical contractor license from the state construction industry licensing board;
(4) If inspecting for compliance with the International Fuel Gas Code, the inspector shall be certified from the International Code Council (ICC) as a mechanical or plumbing inspector or a conditioned air contractor, journeyman plumber, or master plumber license from the state construction industry licensing board;
(5) If inspecting for compliance with the International Mechanical Code or the mechanical portion of the International Residential Code for One- and Two-Family Dwellings, the inspector shall be certified by the International Code Council (ICC) as a mechanical inspector or a conditioned air contractor license from the state construction industry licensing board;
(6) If inspecting for compliance with the International Plumbing Code or the plumbing portion of the International Residential Code for One- and Two-Family Dwellings, the inspector shall be certified by the International Code Council (ICC) as a plumbing inspector or a journeyman plumber or master plumber license from the state construction licensing board;
(7) If inspecting for compliance with any portion of the International Residential Code for One- and Two-Family Dwellings, the inspector shall be certified by the International Code Council (ICC) as a one- and two-family dwelling inspector;
(8) If inspecting for compliance with the Georgia Accessibility Code, the inspector shall be certified by the International Code Council (ICC) as an accessibility inspector; and
(9) If inspecting for compliance with the International Property Maintenance Code, the inspector shall be certified by the International Code Council (ICC) as a property maintenance and housing inspector.
A qualified inspector may perform any inspection required by the applicable codes including but not limited to inspections for footings, foundations, concrete slabs, framing, electrical, plumbing, heating ventilation and air conditioning (HVAC), or any and all other inspections necessary or required for the issuance of a certificate of occupancy or completion.
(Ord. No. 2014-004, § 1(Exh. A), 4-7-14)

